# supa registry — the ONLY thing you maintain by hand: name -> project repo root.
# Copy this file to `supa.registry` (same dir) and edit it for your machine.
#
# Format (one per line):   name|path
#   * name  — what you type:  supa up <name>          (a friendly alias)
#   * path  — the repo root.  supa auto-finds supabase/config.toml under it
#             (at the root, or under apps/<x>/, or examples/<x>/) and reads the
#             docker label (project_id) and live ports straight from that file.
#
# Path rules (cross-platform):
#   * A leading ~ expands to your home dir on every OS.
#   * Use forward slashes even on Windows (C:/code/web works).
#   * Absolute paths work too.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# Override this file's location with SUPA_REGISTRY, or its dir with SUPA_HOME.

web|~/code/web
api|~/code/api
